* #13072000 "Oral applicator"
  * ^definition = "Administration device for administering a liquid or semi-solid pharmaceutical form to the oral cavity. This term may be used to describe an oral syringe in cases where there is a risk of administration error, e.g. where a similar product is often administered by injection, such as with vaccines. It may contain one or more components necessary for the preparation of the final product (e.g. the solvent), but it does not contain the final preparation or all of its components; in such cases, use 'Pre-filled oral applicator' instead."
